  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The length of a given cylindrical wire is increased to double of its original length. The percentage increase in the resistance of the wire will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "300",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As volume is constant, so, length doubled and area reduces to half.</p><p>Resistance of a wire is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi></math>&nbsp;is resistivity of a material.</p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>So percentage increase in the resistance will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
